WEBVTT

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:06.802
Now, a miracle is about to be
created upon this planet.

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:08.531
I'm sorry.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:10.838
I'm really sorry.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:15.178
I'm really happy about
the way you feel about me.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:16.271
But...

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:18.846
...right now...

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.854
Don't tell me this is about...

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.822
This has nothing to do with Chris!

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.060
Then...

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.084
...then why?

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.526
I...

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:31.491
...just don't want to...

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:38.334
I just don't want to put you
in any more danger.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:45.707
Humans are so constrained.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.782
They are bound not only...

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:52.047
...by the words they speak, but
also by the words in their minds.

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:56.289
The more words they put together...

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:59.281
...the more misunderstandings
they create.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:00.787
Then, why?

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:04.192
Why do people depend on words?

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.762
Maybe it's because they are lonely.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.065
They're so afraid of being alone.

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:16.065
They want others
to know about them...

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.411
...so they make words.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:21.548
But for me...

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:24.551
...no matter how many
people are around...

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:27.611
...and no matter how many
people may be close to me...

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:35.251
...it's so much sadder if I can't
communicate what's in my heart.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:40.688
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:59.145
Do you think we can
go on without the TI- 2?

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.813
We were deployed here
because we can.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:02.755
Besides...

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.723
...we're only here to
deal with the little ones.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.497
Raaja response approaching.

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.799
Start up defense system
immediately.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:13.766
Roger.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.464
Starting up.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.640
Good morning.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:25.606
Good morning.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:32.082
I hope you're not going to
feed me that brown rice, Mom.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.612
You can go along with
your little sister on this, can't you?

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:37.980
No way.

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:41.989
I want the Ebisuya
corn flakes with nuts.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.766
If you keep going on about health...

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.132
...your boyfriend will run away.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.403
I'm off.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.609
Now, Kaine and Juna...

00:02:56.609 --> 00:03:00.046
...it's awfully troublesome preparing
different meals. I wish you'd stop this.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:03.249
It's creepy having siblings
always eat and think...

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.648
...the same things.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:09.186
It's coming.

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:17.788
Flick back!

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:34.807
Episode 8: The Distant Rain

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:52.157
Aren't you going to eat that?
lt'll get cold.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:54.365
Uh, right.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.243
Ah, yeah.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.577
I know what you're thinking.

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:07.280
You're thinking how meddlesome
it is for me to lie...

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.115
...in order to bring you here.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.207
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:14.053
But looking at it from
my point of view...

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:17.284
...I can't help but get
involved with you two.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.593
I don't want to waste it,
so I'm going to eat it!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:27.700
Hey!

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.997
It's mine now!

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:56.095
Hey, what's going on here?

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.620
Well, uh, it's uh...

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:08.241
That's dangerous, too, huh?

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:08.832
What?

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.413
To me, it's my favorite food...

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.948
...but to you it's dangerous,
isn't it?

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:16.915
Well...

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.352
Then, we're in the same boat.

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.754
You put me in danger...

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.484
...and I'm putting
you in danger right now.

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.516
This makes us even.

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:33.132
Come on, come on.

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:36.124
I don't know what this is about,
but it does seem like a waste.

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:49.272
I'm sorry.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.825
Oshima...

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.454
Hey.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:29.989
I wonder...

00:06:29.989 --> 00:06:34.050
...if I can have Oshima's.

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:37.025
Okay.

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.055
Thanks.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:51.766
I guess I was
meddlesome today.

00:06:52.145 --> 00:06:56.206
But I really do appreciate
your concern for me.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:57.546
Really.

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.128
What's the situation?

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:12.825
In France, there's a spread in the
infestation of white scale insects.

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:17.069
The EU nations are on the verge
of banning French imports...

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:19.537
...due to the danger of bringing
in the pestilence.

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:23.265
There was a large Pre-Raaja
Reaction in the United States.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:27.201
They're expecting devastating
consequences for the wheat harvest.

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:30.950
The major agricultural producers
have ignored our warnings...

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.578
...and have cornered the
livestock feed market.

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:35.087
If the advanced nations...

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:37.890
...were to reduce their consumption
of meat even a little...

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.415
...world hunger could be eliminated.

00:07:40.927 --> 00:07:43.225
They don't have to go that far.

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:46.432
All that has to be done is to change
the international distribution...

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:47.660
...of food products.

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:51.270
Even if we were able to save
those children from hunger...

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.873
...it would mean higher costs
for the advanced nations.

00:07:53.873 --> 00:07:56.501
A nation can be so unimpassioned
about these things.

00:07:57.643 --> 00:07:59.440
Have you seen it before?

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:03.407
The innocent look on children's
faces as they die of starvation.

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:25.071
What?

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:26.973
At least knock, huh?

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:27.837
I did.

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:44.383
What do you want?

00:08:57.637 --> 00:09:00.299
General Psychology

00:10:08.374 --> 00:10:09.342
Hello.

00:10:09.342 --> 00:10:10.536
Oshima residence.

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:14.643
Hello?

00:10:17.817 --> 00:10:19.045
Hello?

00:10:21.854 --> 00:10:24.152
Huh? Is this Juna?

00:10:24.957 --> 00:10:27.357
Can't you tell with your
call display?

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:30.363
The call display is blocked.

00:10:30.363 --> 00:10:31.227
Oops.

00:10:31.964 --> 00:10:32.828
I made a mistake.

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:34.667
Really?

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:35.827
Really.

00:10:37.203 --> 00:10:38.033
Whatever.

00:10:40.573 --> 00:10:41.597
So, what do you want?

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:46.171
Hello?

00:10:48.514 --> 00:10:49.981
Hello?

00:10:53.853 --> 00:10:54.717
Huh?

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.581
What were you doing
just now?

00:11:00.893 --> 00:11:02.228
What?

00:11:02.228 --> 00:11:04.397
I was eating noodles
and watching TV.

00:11:04.397 --> 00:11:05.398
Again?

00:11:05.398 --> 00:11:07.099
What do you mean?

00:11:07.099 --> 00:11:08.691
Are you going to give me hell again?

00:11:10.069 --> 00:11:11.730
I wasn't planning on it.

00:11:12.238 --> 00:11:14.001
I just, well...

00:11:14.507 --> 00:11:15.701
...I wanted to apologize.

00:11:16.308 --> 00:11:17.172
Apologize?

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:18.972
About the ring.

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:21.378
Don't worry about it.

00:11:22.214 --> 00:11:23.349
I'm sorry.

00:11:23.349 --> 00:11:24.950
It's okay.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.214
I know how you feel now.

00:11:27.553 --> 00:11:29.555
I wish you wouldn't
put it that way.

00:11:29.555 --> 00:11:31.123
That's not what I meant.

00:11:31.123 --> 00:11:32.425
Even if I forced the issue...

00:11:32.425 --> 00:11:34.825
...you still wouldn't wear
that ring anyway.

00:11:35.661 --> 00:11:39.597
If you don't want to wear
the ring, what's the point?

00:11:39.932 --> 00:11:42.924
It's not that I don't want to
wear the ring.

00:11:46.072 --> 00:11:47.334
I'm sorry.

00:11:48.274 --> 00:11:49.642
Don't worry about it.

00:11:49.642 --> 00:11:51.944
I have to apologize to you, too.

00:11:51.944 --> 00:11:55.505
I'm sorry for dragging you
to a place like that.

00:11:56.148 --> 00:11:59.379
But wasn't Sayuri the one
who put us up to that?

00:11:59.585 --> 00:12:01.849
But I got suckered into it.

00:12:02.188 --> 00:12:05.157
It's the same with me.

00:12:05.458 --> 00:12:06.982
Why did you go, then?

00:12:07.727 --> 00:12:08.853
How about you?

00:12:10.396 --> 00:12:12.762
Because I wanted to see you.

00:12:16.769 --> 00:12:17.667
Me too.

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:20.732
I wonder why...

00:12:21.273 --> 00:12:24.208
...it's easier to be honest
on a cell phone.

00:12:24.744 --> 00:12:25.642
That's true.

00:12:26.712 --> 00:12:27.913
Even though we're apart...

00:12:27.913 --> 00:12:30.347
...it's almost like we're together.

00:12:33.919 --> 00:12:35.978
Juna? Juna?

00:12:37.089 --> 00:12:38.556
Hey, what's wrong?

00:12:59.945 --> 00:13:02.277
Hello? Hello?

00:13:02.782 --> 00:13:03.578
Tokio!

00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:08.220
Nourishment from the fruits
of the land.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:11.724
I've grown to be tasty, so
go ahead and eat me.

00:13:11.724 --> 00:13:15.319
Apples and oranges,
carrots and parsley...

00:13:15.628 --> 00:13:19.231
...tomatoes and cabbage,
watercress and green peppers...

00:13:19.231 --> 00:13:22.868
Appare! Appare!
Appare of the land!

00:13:22.868 --> 00:13:26.038
Another Appare
day for me!

00:13:26.038 --> 00:13:26.970
It's delicious!

00:13:27.306 --> 00:13:31.572
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:13:40.352 --> 00:13:41.614
It's been one hour.

00:13:52.731 --> 00:13:55.097
Do you think Chris is useless now?!

00:13:55.835 --> 00:13:58.770
I wish you wouldn't read my mind
without my permission.

00:13:59.238 --> 00:14:01.607
As a violation of the
TI psychic agreement...

00:14:01.607 --> 00:14:03.809
...that's cause for dismissal,
you know.

00:14:03.809 --> 00:14:05.640
There's no way you can...

00:14:06.045 --> 00:14:06.739
I wonder.

00:14:07.279 --> 00:14:09.615
There's the incident
in the underground shrine.

00:14:09.615 --> 00:14:13.847
The medical staff have
been taking precautions.

00:14:14.286 --> 00:14:16.055
At least that's what we thought.

00:14:16.055 --> 00:14:18.057
But, without Chris...

00:14:18.057 --> 00:14:20.685
...we get very stressed
out in the field.

00:14:21.594 --> 00:14:24.062
Then do it without Chris.

00:14:25.364 --> 00:14:29.068
I can at least read that, even if
I don't have psychic ability.

00:14:29.068 --> 00:14:32.231
Your world is too small
and too simple.

00:14:32.538 --> 00:14:34.563
So what if you were able
to read me?

00:14:35.174 --> 00:14:36.072
Indeed.

00:14:37.076 --> 00:14:40.170
So what if I was able to read you?

00:14:43.515 --> 00:14:45.642
Why are you here?

00:14:45.985 --> 00:14:46.883
Huh?

00:14:47.319 --> 00:14:50.389
What's wrong with me
being in my own room?

00:14:50.389 --> 00:14:52.050
What are you talking about?

00:14:52.758 --> 00:14:54.126
Your room?

00:14:54.126 --> 00:14:54.490
Huh?

00:15:00.165 --> 00:15:01.767
No way...

00:15:01.767 --> 00:15:03.359
Is this really...

00:15:04.236 --> 00:15:05.601
...Tokio's room?

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.504
How are you doing, Tokio?

00:15:17.216 --> 00:15:20.117
I'll leave this here for you.

00:15:23.789 --> 00:15:25.780
Who was that just now?

00:15:26.458 --> 00:15:28.517
Did you hear her voice?

00:15:28.994 --> 00:15:30.529
That was my mom.

00:15:30.529 --> 00:15:31.764
Your mom?!

00:15:31.764 --> 00:15:32.958
Yeah, my mom.

00:15:33.666 --> 00:15:36.134
Well, not my real mom.

00:15:36.435 --> 00:15:38.203
She's my dad's second wife.

00:15:38.203 --> 00:15:40.865
Really? She's so young.

00:15:41.507 --> 00:15:43.208
How could you tell?

00:15:43.208 --> 00:15:44.368
It's like you saw her.

00:15:44.543 --> 00:15:45.878
What are you talking about?

00:15:45.878 --> 00:15:47.313
I can see it all.

00:15:47.313 --> 00:15:48.610
I'm right here.

00:15:51.517 --> 00:15:52.551
What's the matter?

00:15:52.551 --> 00:15:55.281
- Hello? Hello?
- It's like I've left my body.

00:15:56.488 --> 00:15:57.580
Which means...

00:15:59.959 --> 00:16:02.928
Huh? Hey!

00:16:02.928 --> 00:16:03.952
What's going on?

00:16:04.296 --> 00:16:07.199
Oh, no! It's like I've died again.

00:16:07.199 --> 00:16:08.166
Huh?

00:16:08.367 --> 00:16:11.770
Now, if you've died,
who am I talking to, then?

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:13.863
This isn't some kind of
comic act.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:19.077
If my voice can be heard
through your cell phone...

00:16:20.679 --> 00:16:23.315
...is it just that I left my body...

00:16:23.315 --> 00:16:25.943
...and my real body is still
talking on the phone?

00:16:26.218 --> 00:16:28.379
Hey, what's the matter?

00:16:28.654 --> 00:16:29.450
Which means that...

00:16:30.856 --> 00:16:31.413
What?

00:16:33.792 --> 00:16:37.159
It means that I'm still alive.

00:16:38.897 --> 00:16:41.867
If you're going to go on like this,
I'm going to hang up.

00:16:41.867 --> 00:16:43.562
Huh? No.
No, no, no...!

00:16:43.902 --> 00:16:44.636
Don't hang up!

00:16:44.636 --> 00:16:45.671
Please, please, please.

00:16:45.671 --> 00:16:48.265
I'm begging you!

00:16:48.574 --> 00:16:49.973
Don't hang up. Don't hang up.

00:16:51.443 --> 00:16:53.741
You sure are a funny one.

00:16:54.079 --> 00:16:55.637
Hey.

00:16:57.516 --> 00:16:58.642
That ring...

00:16:59.551 --> 00:17:00.245
What?

00:17:00.586 --> 00:17:02.451
Uh, nothing.

00:17:03.155 --> 00:17:03.712
Right.

00:17:04.423 --> 00:17:06.925
Hey, do you want to go
somewhere sometime?

00:17:06.925 --> 00:17:07.823
What?

00:17:08.227 --> 00:17:10.295
Does this have something
to do with the ring?

00:17:10.295 --> 00:17:12.923
Huh? How could you tell?

00:17:16.268 --> 00:17:18.862
I can tell, at least that much.

00:17:19.705 --> 00:17:21.639
So, where do you want to go?

00:17:21.874 --> 00:17:23.175
Uh, I don't know.

00:17:23.175 --> 00:17:24.199
Let's see.

00:17:29.314 --> 00:17:29.973
The sea.

00:17:30.182 --> 00:17:31.615
Let's go to the sea.

00:17:34.887 --> 00:17:36.787
Meriken Burger!

00:17:37.022 --> 00:17:37.954
Just kidding.

00:17:40.793 --> 00:17:42.761
I guess I'll just have
to eat their food.

00:17:42.761 --> 00:17:44.592
We don't really have to go there.

00:17:45.731 --> 00:17:49.724
I just want to sit down and
have a meal with you.

00:17:50.102 --> 00:17:51.228
Tokio...

00:17:53.872 --> 00:17:55.339
Kobe Walker Magazine
Best Health Food Restaurants

00:17:59.645 --> 00:18:01.914
Hey, I can't believe this!

00:18:01.914 --> 00:18:02.778
What?

00:18:03.015 --> 00:18:04.539
I can see right through you.

00:18:06.151 --> 00:18:08.921
But I just love you...

00:18:08.921 --> 00:18:09.751
What?!

00:18:10.189 --> 00:18:12.214
I just love you.

00:18:27.339 --> 00:18:28.774
But lately...

00:18:28.774 --> 00:18:33.905
...it feels like we're so
distant from each other.

00:18:34.613 --> 00:18:35.773
It makes me worry.

00:18:39.351 --> 00:18:40.443
I'm sorry...

00:18:40.919 --> 00:18:42.784
...for making you feel so bad.

00:18:43.755 --> 00:18:46.417
I just don't know...

00:18:47.159 --> 00:18:49.428
...how I'm supposed to
deal with this.

00:18:49.428 --> 00:18:51.658
I think I just need a little time.

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:53.932
Time, huh?

00:18:53.932 --> 00:18:57.493
I just want to spend time
with you.

00:18:57.803 --> 00:19:01.239
But we're spending
time together now.

00:19:01.573 --> 00:19:03.742
That's how you might feel...

00:19:03.742 --> 00:19:06.074
...but it's different for me.

00:19:07.012 --> 00:19:07.569
Oh, no.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.945
My battery's about to run out.

00:19:10.716 --> 00:19:11.842
I'm always...

00:19:12.184 --> 00:19:12.616
Huh?

00:19:12.885 --> 00:19:15.046
I'm always with you.

00:19:15.787 --> 00:19:16.685
Can I really...

00:19:17.556 --> 00:19:19.751
...can I really believe you?

00:19:24.196 --> 00:19:25.094
Yeah.

00:19:30.169 --> 00:19:30.897
What?

00:19:32.771 --> 00:19:35.706
This is my room.
I guess I came back.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.474
Tokio...

00:19:47.719 --> 00:19:49.084
Michael Resnick.

00:19:49.488 --> 00:19:49.954
Yes.

00:19:50.556 --> 00:19:52.217
Sanae Yamamoto.

00:19:52.624 --> 00:19:53.022
Yes.

00:19:53.725 --> 00:19:54.384
All personnel...

00:19:54.593 --> 00:19:55.491
...board the aircraft.

00:19:58.564 --> 00:20:01.567
The troops are getting
quite exhausted.

00:20:01.567 --> 00:20:04.136
The situation is unfolding
too quickly.

00:20:04.136 --> 00:20:06.205
The world may be
slowly destroying itself...

00:20:06.205 --> 00:20:08.537
...no matter how hard we work.

00:20:09.107 --> 00:20:11.667
What do you think will
happen to the world?

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:31.925
It looks like it's
going to rain again.

00:20:43.642 --> 00:20:44.438
All right!

00:21:01.226 --> 00:21:02.454
I just can't do it.

00:21:02.861 --> 00:21:04.988
No matter what.

00:21:06.031 --> 00:21:08.761
She's making too big of
a deal about burgers.

00:21:08.967 --> 00:21:10.161
But still...

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:12.965
It's just food, after all.

00:21:13.372 --> 00:21:14.031
Huh?

00:21:15.073 --> 00:21:18.076
But Juna's always been like that.

00:21:18.076 --> 00:21:19.845
She can be so intense.

00:21:19.845 --> 00:21:21.437
Yeah, I suppose.

00:21:21.947 --> 00:21:23.315
Tokio?

00:21:23.315 --> 00:21:24.782
Sayuri?

00:21:25.083 --> 00:21:25.947
Why?

00:21:26.852 --> 00:21:30.055
You sure eat a lot.

00:21:30.055 --> 00:21:33.625
Don't tell Juna that
she eats a lot.

00:21:33.625 --> 00:21:36.428
An appetite is the enemy
of a woman.

00:21:36.428 --> 00:21:37.963
Enemy or not...

00:21:37.963 --> 00:21:40.557
...it's best to enjoy the
food you like.

00:21:42.334 --> 00:21:45.633
So, what do you like about Juna?

00:21:45.837 --> 00:21:47.205
What is it all of a sudden?

00:21:47.205 --> 00:21:51.869
I mean, you've been complaining
about Juna for a while now.

00:21:54.813 --> 00:21:56.481
I don't know.

00:21:56.481 --> 00:21:58.583
It's hard to put my finger on it.

00:21:58.583 --> 00:21:59.106
Huh?

00:21:59.751 --> 00:22:01.275
Well, think about it.

00:22:01.753 --> 00:22:05.416
When people fall in love,
people aren't like parts...

00:22:05.991 --> 00:22:08.226
...so if you ask why I like someone...

00:22:08.226 --> 00:22:10.329
...I can't tell you which part it is
that I love.

00:22:10.329 --> 00:22:13.765
Whether it's the eyes,
or the legs, or whatever...

00:22:16.134 --> 00:22:18.796
You like her that much...

00:22:23.208 --> 00:22:25.267
Hey, it's raining again.

00:22:27.679 --> 00:22:30.782
It rains and then stops.

00:22:30.782 --> 00:22:32.272
I wish it would just decide.

00:22:33.018 --> 00:22:34.076
Yeah.

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:43.261
They say the rain...

00:22:43.261 --> 00:22:47.493
...is the tears of a woman
suffering from unrequited love.

00:22:49.835 --> 00:22:50.665
Really.

00:22:51.703 --> 00:22:54.331
Hey, can I have one of your fries?

00:22:55.474 --> 00:22:56.498
Here it goes.

00:22:58.744 --> 00:23:00.812
Juna can't be helped.

00:23:00.812 --> 00:23:04.216
She says she sees
how the food was created...

00:23:04.216 --> 00:23:08.243
...but she doesn't understand
that the food wants to be eaten.

00:23:09.221 --> 00:23:10.822
I guess.

00:23:10.822 --> 00:23:12.891
Maybe this one right here...

00:23:12.891 --> 00:23:15.451
...is begging to be eaten.

00:23:16.161 --> 00:23:18.797
Without even thinking about that...

00:23:18.797 --> 00:23:22.392
...she decides what you should eat
and what you shouldn't eat.

00:23:23.869 --> 00:23:26.963
She doesn't know
how the food feels. Right?

00:23:34.346 --> 00:23:36.837
Sayuri, what's the matter?

00:23:37.616 --> 00:23:38.810
H-hey...!

00:23:45.023 --> 00:23:45.751
Hey, wait!

00:23:46.725 --> 00:23:48.126
Don't misunderstand me.

00:23:48.126 --> 00:23:50.492
I'm Juna's friend, you know.

00:23:50.862 --> 00:23:51.794
Sayuri...

00:23:58.670 --> 00:24:05.510
Quietly and sadly

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:13.246
You hum my favorite song

00:24:13.318 --> 00:24:17.956
I have to go, or no one will save

00:24:17.956 --> 00:24:21.193
The boy who wandered

00:24:21.193 --> 00:24:25.630
Into the deep darkness

00:24:25.630 --> 00:24:30.435
With love alone, I will go

00:24:30.435 --> 00:24:33.371
No matter where you are

00:24:33.371 --> 00:24:37.909
I will go running straight to you

00:24:37.909 --> 00:24:42.814
So, in a loud voice

00:24:42.814 --> 00:24:49.378
Call out my name again and again

00:24:50.255 --> 00:24:53.158
Quicker than anyone

00:24:53.158 --> 00:24:59.264
I'll be there

00:24:59.264 --> 00:25:12.075
Close to your side
